WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en
Style:
::cue(c.colorCCCCCC) { color: rgb(204,204,204);
 }
::cue(c.colorEEEEEE) { color: rgb(238,238,238);
 }
::cue(c.cyan) { color: cyan; }
::cue(c.yellow) { color: yellow; }
##

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.640 line:91%
Do you remember that
container ship, the <i>Ever Given</i>,

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:05.400 line:91%
that got stuck in the
Suez Canal back in 2021?

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.080 line:91%
The final report
into what happened

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:09.040 line:91%
came out a few months ago,
as I record this,

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:11.760 line:91%
and there were a lot of
things that went wrong.

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:13.120 line:85%
It was travelling too fast,

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:14.640 line:91%
there were communications
problems between

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:16.160 line:85%
the crew and the local pilots,

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:18.800 line:91%
and there was the
<i>bank effect</i>.

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:20.880 line:91%
There are two ways
to learn what that is.

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:23.000 line:91%
You can get the
theoretical explanation

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.360 line:91%
that big ships get
sucked to the sidewalls

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:26.560 line:85%
by pressure differences

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:28.560 line:91%
when travelling
at speed along canals.

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:30.480 line:91%
But if that seems
a bit abstract,

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:32.360 line:85%
you can learn it hands-on.

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:33.680 line:85%
Because this is the

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:36.960 line:91%
Port Iława Ship Handling
Research and Training Centre

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:38.200 line:85%
in the north of Poland.

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:39.560 line:85%
And this is one of the places

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:41.600 line:91%
where the folks who
steer those big ships

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:42.880 line:85%
learn how to do it.

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:45.360 line:91%
Just to be clear, I'm not
getting a full training course.

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:46.920 line:91%
That takes days
and includes

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:49.400 line:91%
a huge amount of theory work
and study as well.

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:51.880 line:91%
I'm just going to drive a
miniature container ship

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:53.960 line:91%
for a lap around
the lake, and...

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:56.680 line:91%
hopefully not get it
stuck in the Suez Canal.

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:02.080 line:91%
<c.yellow>We have started our
training activity in 1980.</c>

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:07.680 line:91%
<c.yellow>In the '90s, we have moved from
the old lake towards this one,</c>

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:11.880 line:91%
<c.yellow>and practically first training
here was realized in 1991,</c>

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:14.240 line:85%
<c.yellow>more or less 30 years ago.</c>

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:17.160 line:91%
<c.yellow>We are performing
training in ship handling.</c>

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:19.920 line:91%
<c.yellow>We have a lot of
different mockups</c>

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:22.120 line:91%
<c.yellow>presenting
different waterways.</c>

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:26.720 line:91%
<c.yellow>Everything was built using
exactly the same scale, 1:24.</c>

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:29.400 line:91%
<c.yellow>Deep waters,
shallow waters,</c>

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:32.320 line:91%
<c.yellow>different restrictions,
rivers, canals.</c>

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:34.000 line:85%
<c.yellow>And what is more important?</c>

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.520 line:85%
<c.yellow>Of course, ship models.</c>

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:36.920 line:85%
Permission to come aboard?

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:38.400 line:91%
<c.cyan>Granted.</c>
<i>(laughs)</i>

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:40.240 line:85%
Okay.

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:41.480 line:85%
This is bigger

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:43.360 line:91%
than I thought
it was going to be.

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:45.920 line:91%
<c.cyan>It's one of the
biggest in the world.</c>

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:47.520 line:85%
<c.cyan>400 metre ship.</c>

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:49.200 line:85%
400 metre?

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:51.480 line:91%
Scaled down 1:24,
that's still...

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:53.040 line:85%
<c.cyan>16 and a half.</c>

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:55.720 line:91%
That's— Okay,
this is big, cool.

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:57.400 line:91%
<c.cyan>We can proceed.
Dead slow ahead.</c>

00:01:57.400 --> 00:01:59.200 line:91%
<c.colorEEEEEE>So dead slow ahead?</c>
<c.cyan>Yep.</c>

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:02.840 line:91%
<c.cyan>And steady as she goes.
Forward.</c>

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:05.720 line:91%
I assume that means just
keep it going straight, okay.

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:07.720 line:91%
<c.cyan>These are the
tugboat simulators.</c>

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:09.520 line:91%
Oh, I don't feel
guilty about you...

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:11.360 line:91%
You've taken
the controls here.

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:12.840 line:85%
I'd be on tugboats going out.

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:14.800 line:91%
I was meant to be asking
all sorts of questions here,

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:18.760 line:91%
and I'm just slightly nervous
about driving a tiny boat.

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:20.520 line:85%
<c.cyan>It's not a tiny boat.</c>

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:23.040 line:85%
<c.cyan>It's a 400m container ship.</c>

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:25.040 line:91%
Yep. So you have
controls there

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:27.360 line:91%
that simulate the effect
of tugs on the boat.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:28.520 line:85%
<c.cyan>Right, four tugs.</c>

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:30.720 line:91%
<c.cyan>You may make a
rather hard to port.</c>

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:32.480 line:85%
Hard to port?

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:34.120 line:85%
I don't know why...

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.440 line:91%
but I thought I was
going to spin that

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:36.720 line:91%
like the wheel of a
pirate ship,

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:38.760 line:91%
<c.colorEEEEEE>and it's just a...</c>
<c.cyan>Yeah.</c>

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:41.000 line:91%
Alright, so
what's our plan now?

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:43.960 line:91%
<c.cyan>Okay, so now we can go
through the lock if you like.</c>

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:45.680 line:85%
Yeah, absolutely.

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:48.840 line:91%
<c.cyan>Basically we go that direction,
south of the island.</c>

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:50.400 line:91%
I feel like I need
to go left here.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:52.920 line:91%
<c.cyan>Yeah, make it port 10.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Port, not left.</c>

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:55.000 line:85%
<c.yellow>We have had, in our history,</c>

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:59.520 line:91%
<c.yellow>more than 6,000 pilots,
masters, and chief officers</c>

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:01.480 line:85%
<c.yellow>from more than 50 countries.</c>

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:06.160 line:85%
<c.yellow>On average, 220–230 a year.</c>

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:08.400 line:85%
<c.yellow>We have beginners,</c>

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:11.200 line:91%
<c.yellow>but we have also very
experienced masters.</c>

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:13.840 line:91%
<c.cyan>Because the lock
is very shallow...</c>

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:15.080 line:91%
<c.colorEEEEEE>Yeah.</c>
<c.cyan>We will have</c>

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:17.520 line:91%
<c.cyan>only 2cm of water
under the keel.</c>

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:19.960 line:91%
<c.cyan>If we have too high a speed,
we touch the bottom.</c>

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:21.960 line:91%
So the faster I go
in shallow water,

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:25.000 line:91%
the more the boat is going to
get sucked down to the ground.

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:26.600 line:91%
<c.cyan>More squat
you have, yeah.</c>

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:28.880 line:91%
<c.cyan>We have to come
in line with the lock.</c>

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:30.960 line:91%
<c.colorEEEEEE>Oh!</c>
<c.cyan>Sooner we do that,</c>

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:34.120 line:91%
<c.cyan>more time we have to apply
any correction if necessary.</c>

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:39.440 line:91%
That is such a tight
spot to navigate through.

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:41.160 line:91%
<c.cyan>Hard to starboard
for a while.</c>

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:42.920 line:91%
<c.colorEEEEEE>Hard to star—</c>
<c.cyan>Starboard, starboard.</c>

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:45.440 line:91%
The minute I feel like
I've got this...

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:47.040 line:85%
It's all going to fall apart.

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:47.960 line:85%
Uh, midships?

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:49.200 line:91%
<c.cyan>Yes, please.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Yep.</c>

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:51.440 line:91%
<c.colorEEEEEE>And starboard— yep.</c>
<c.cyan>Starboard 20.</c>

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:53.320 line:85%
And midships, yep.

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:55.480 line:91%
Oh, I think I've
overcorrected there!

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:56.840 line:85%
There's some very strong work

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:59.200 line:91%
being done by the
tugboats here, thank you.

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:01.120 line:85%
We have no clearance here!

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:02.720 line:85%
I feel like starboard slightly?

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:04.640 line:91%
<c.cyan>Yeah, starboard 20.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Starboard 20.</c>

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:05.880 line:85%
(winces)

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:08.200 line:91%
I can't see how
close we are there.

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:10.000 line:91%
<c.colorEEEEEE>Did we clear that?</c>
<c.cyan>Yes.</c>

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:11.360 line:91%
<c.colorEEEEEE>I think we cleared that.</c>
<c.cyan>Yes!</c>

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:13.960 line:91%
<i>(wheezes)</i> Again,
solid tugboat work.

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:15.520 line:85%
Midships, surely.

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:17.720 line:91%
<c.cyan>Starboard 20.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Okay!</c>

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:20.200 line:91%
<c.yellow>The basic training
program takes five days.</c>

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:24.040 line:85%
<c.yellow>A linear scale, 1:24, means</c>

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:28.240 line:91%
<c.yellow>that timescale is equal
to more or less five.</c>

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:29.880 line:85%
<c.yellow>It means everything happens</c>

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:32.000 line:91%
<c.yellow>five times faster
than in reality.</c>

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:35.200 line:91%
<c.yellow>And feeling for a ship
may be affected.</c>

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:36.920 line:85%
<c.yellow>It's a disadvantage.</c>

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:40.000 line:91%
<c.yellow>But on the other hand,
five days of training</c>

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:43.920 line:91%
<c.yellow>will correspond to 25 days
of training in reality.</c>

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:46.200 line:91%
<c.cyan>Hard to starboard.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Hard to starboard.</c>

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:47.840 line:91%
I'm more the helmsman
than the captain

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:49.320 line:85%
at this point, thank you.

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:50.400 line:85%
<c.cyan>Hard to port again.</c>

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:52.800 line:91%
Hard to port.
Left hand down a bit!

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:55.440 line:91%
<c.cyan>Okay, I think we
can make half ahead.</c>

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:56.480 line:85%
Half ahead.

00:04:57.440 --> 00:04:59.240 line:85%
We are clear of the lock.

00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:00.000 line:85%
<c.cyan>Oh, yeah.</c>

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:02.520 line:85%
Phew!

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:04.520 line:91%
<c.cyan>Full ahead.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Full ahead!</c>

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:06.520 line:85%
<c.colorCCCCCC><i>(both laughing)</i></c>

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:08.480 line:91%
Did I need to slam that
forward so dramatically?

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:10.120 line:85%
Absolutely not, but...

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:13.040 line:91%
<c.yellow>Our first models
were really very simple.</c>

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:14.520 line:85%
<c.yellow>Nothing inside.</c>

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:16.360 line:91%
<c.yellow>Just wheel,
engine telegraph,</c>

00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:17.520 line:85%
<c.yellow>and that's it.</c>

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:19.200 line:85%
<c.yellow>And step by step...</c>

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:23.160 line:91%
<c.yellow>we have started to add
different facilities.</c>

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:25.320 line:85%
<c.yellow>We have electronic navigation.</c>

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:28.320 line:91%
<c.yellow>It means a very precise
GPS system,</c>

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:32.280 line:91%
<c.yellow>which allows to measure a
given ship model trajectory</c>

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:35.720 line:91%
<c.yellow>with precision equal to
one, maybe two centimetres.</c>

00:05:35.720 --> 00:05:37.960 line:91%
Suddenly the nerves
have gone.

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:41.040 line:85%
Open ocean. Open lake.

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:43.120 line:91%
<c.cyan>Starboard 10.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Starboard 10.</c>

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:44.680 line:91%
'Cause you've
got to cancel out

00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:46.360 line:91%
<c.colorEEEEEE>what you've just given it, right?</c>
<c.cyan>Yeah.</c>

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:48.480 line:91%
We're still going
quite strongly to port

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:50.360 line:91%
<c.colorEEEEEE>just because that input from...</c>
<c.cyan>The wind.</c>

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:52.200 line:91%
<c.colorEEEEEE>Ages ago, and the wind?</c>
<c.cyan>Due to the wind, yeah.</c>

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:54.680 line:91%
I'm amazed how much
the wind is affecting this.

00:05:54.680 --> 00:05:57.320 line:91%
<c.cyan>You have to imagine
that such a ship, fully loaded,</c>

00:05:57.320 --> 00:05:59.640 line:91%
<c.cyan>has about 20,000
square metres</c>

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:01.000 line:85%
<c.cyan>with the windage area.</c>

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:02.680 line:85%
(heavy sigh)

00:06:02.680 --> 00:06:05.520 line:91%
<c.yellow>Everything during
exercises is measured,</c>

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:08.960 line:91%
<c.yellow>sent to our classroom,
and in case of problems,</c>

00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:11.320 line:85%
<c.yellow>we can discuss step by step,</c>

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:14.640 line:91%
<c.yellow>and we can show where
mistakes were made.</c>

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:16.920 line:91%
Ooh! ...I'm sorry, I got
distracted by a cormorant.

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:18.160 line:85%
<c.colorCCCCCC><i>(both chuckle)</i></c>

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:20.520 line:91%
<c.yellow>Current, especially in
the case of shallow water,</c>

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:22.040 line:85%
<c.yellow>is a big problem.</c>

00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:24.280 line:91%
<c.yellow>It means we have
current generators.</c>

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:28.680 line:91%
<c.yellow>This current velocity can be
changed according to our needs.</c>

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:29.920 line:85%
<c.colorCCCCCC><i>(metal colliding)</i></c>

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:31.840 line:85%
I thought we hit something.

00:06:31.840 --> 00:06:33.640 line:91%
Oh, we did.
That's me, sorry.

00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:35.360 line:91%
<c.cyan>No problem.</c>
<i>(nervous chuckle)</i>

00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:37.680 line:91%
It's not like this thing
has rear-view mirrors.

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:39.560 line:85%
<c.cyan>Okay, half ahead.</c>

00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:40.760 line:85%
Half ahead?

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:42.800 line:91%
We're sailing a
massive container ship

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:43.920 line:85%
down the Suez Canal.

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:46.000 line:91%
Do I need to put a little
bit of rudder in here?

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:49.480 line:91%
<c.cyan>Yeah, it's fine. Now you
have to go behind Varta.</c>

00:06:49.480 --> 00:06:51.840 line:91%
<c.colorEEEEEE>Right.</c>
<c.cyan>You can make a port 10.</c>

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:53.200 line:85%
Port 10, got it.

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:54.920 line:91%
I think we're clear
of the red buoy.

00:06:54.920 --> 00:06:56.560 line:91%
<c.cyan>Midship.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Midships.</c>

00:06:57.600 --> 00:06:59.400 line:91%
<i>(winces)</i>
<c.cyan>No, no, it's clear.</c>

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:02.200 line:91%
<c.colorEEEEEE>Okay. Port 20.</c>
<c.cyan>Port 20.</c>

00:07:02.200 --> 00:07:04.920 line:91%
<c.cyan>Midships.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Midships. Okay.</c>

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:06.240 line:85%
<c.cyan>And a full ahead.</c>

00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:08.200 line:85%
Full ahead, okay!

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:10.120 line:91%
<c.cyan>Starboard 20.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Starboard 20.</c>

00:07:10.120 --> 00:07:12.080 line:91%
<c.cyan>Because we've got to
ease out the turn.</c>

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:13.760 line:91%
<c.cyan>Then you will start
feeling the bank effect</c>

00:07:13.760 --> 00:07:15.200 line:85%
<c.cyan>from the starboard wall.</c>

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:16.480 line:85%
Okay.

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:18.680 line:85%
<c.cyan>Hard to starboard.</c>

00:07:18.680 --> 00:07:20.680 line:91%
So it feels like
I could go midships now.

00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:22.760 line:91%
We should just go straight
down the middle of this canal.

00:07:22.760 --> 00:07:24.240 line:85%
Except...

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:27.080 line:91%
<c.cyan>The bank effect,
you see, bow is coming out.</c>

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:30.240 line:91%
<c.cyan>It means the repulsion
force pushes the bow.</c>

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:32.000 line:91%
<c.cyan>Now you have to make
a hard to starboard.</c>

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:34.000 line:91%
Hard to starboard.
Gah, yeah!

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:36.280 line:91%
I'm being sucked
towards the port wall!

00:07:36.280 --> 00:07:39.080 line:91%
I'm putting full
right lock on here.

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:41.520 line:91%
<c.cyan>Midships.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Midships, okay.</c>

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:42.600 line:85%
<c.cyan>You see, again, it's coming.</c>

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:44.040 line:85%
Yep... it is!

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:45.840 line:91%
<c.cyan>So we have to make
hard to starboard.</c>

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:47.680 line:91%
Hard to starboard, yeah,
if I don't do hard to starboard—

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:49.320 line:91%
<c.cyan>You would have hit this wall.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Yeah.</c>

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:50.920 line:91%
I'm absolutely gonna
ram that if we're not careful.

00:07:50.920 --> 00:07:51.840 line:85%
Yeah.

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:53.280 line:91%
<c.colorEEEEEE>That's so powerful!</c>
<c.cyan>Midships.</c>

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:54.400 line:85%
<c.cyan>Yep.</c>

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:56.880 line:91%
<c.colorEEEEEE>Yeah, hard to starboard.</c>
<c.cyan>Hard to starboard.</c>

00:07:56.880 --> 00:07:57.800 line:85%
I was midships.

00:07:57.800 --> 00:07:59.080 line:91%
We should have been
going straight ahead.

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:00.440 line:91%
<c.colorEEEEEE>And I think...</c>
<c.cyan>I think...</c>

00:08:00.440 --> 00:08:01.680 line:91%
<c.cyan>I have to help you
with that task.</c>

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:02.880 line:91%
Yeah, you're going
to have to help with that.

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:04.280 line:85%
I should've done that earlier.

00:08:05.480 --> 00:08:06.880 line:85%
Everybody down.

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:09.360 line:91%
<c.cyan>Clear.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Oh, cleared?!</c>

00:08:09.360 --> 00:08:11.720 line:91%
<c.cyan>Midship. Hard to port now.</c>
<i>(bewildered laugh)</i>

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:13.200 line:85%
Hard to port.

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:15.360 line:91%
<c.cyan>You were lucky,
one inch clear.</c>

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:18.720 line:91%
That was more luck than
good judgment, that was!

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:21.800 line:91%
<c.yellow>Our research is focused
on ship handling.</c>

00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:24.600 line:91%
<c.yellow>It means interaction
forces, and...</c>

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:26.400 line:85%
<c.yellow>autonomous ships.</c>

00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:28.280 line:85%
<c.yellow>We have started</c>

00:08:28.280 --> 00:08:30.640 line:91%
<c.yellow>realisation of
research programs</c>

00:08:30.640 --> 00:08:33.440 line:91%
<c.yellow>three or four years ago,
because...</c>

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:36.440 line:91%
<c.yellow>autonomous ships
will be really very popular.</c>

00:08:36.440 --> 00:08:39.360 line:91%
<c.yellow>We need at least
ten ships' lengths...</c>

00:08:39.360 --> 00:08:41.680 line:91%
Yeah.
<c.yellow>...to stop the ship.</c>

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:42.960 line:85%
Ten ships' lengths?

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:44.520 line:85%
<c.yellow>And that harbour is here.</c>

00:08:44.520 --> 00:08:45.800 line:91%
Oh, I definitely need
to put some port in.

00:08:45.800 --> 00:08:47.360 line:91%
<c.yellow>Yes. Hard to port.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Port 20.</c>

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:48.440 line:85%
Hard to port, okay.

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:51.080 line:91%
<c.yellow>Everything in case
of our training centre</c>

00:08:51.080 --> 00:08:55.040 line:85%
<c.yellow>is realised in real conditions.</c>

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:57.560 line:91%
<c.yellow>You can feel very well
wind,</c>

00:08:57.560 --> 00:09:00.000 line:91%
<c.yellow>you can feel very well
current,</c>

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:04.160 line:91%
<c.yellow>and everything what deals
with weather conditions.</c>

00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:06.760 line:91%
<c.yellow>Such a situation
does not happen</c>

00:09:06.760 --> 00:09:09.440 line:91%
<c.yellow>in case when using
computer simulators.</c>

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:12.160 line:91%
<c.yellow>And... especially
pilots coming to</c>

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:16.360 line:91%
<c.yellow>our training centre for training
prefer very often to use</c>

00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:19.120 line:91%
<c.yellow>models instead of
computer simulation.</c>

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:21.840 line:91%
Every driver's
instinct in me is going,

00:09:21.840 --> 00:09:24.600 line:91%
"I can just slam it in reverse.
Take it 'round, it'll be fine."

00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:27.200 line:91%
No, it won't.
That's not how this works.

00:09:27.200 --> 00:09:30.080 line:91%
<c.yellow>Collisions really occur
at our training centre.</c>

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:33.680 line:91%
<c.yellow>The main difference regarding
computers and our models</c>

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:36.920 line:91%
<c.yellow>is in computers,
in case of problems,</c>

00:09:36.920 --> 00:09:38.760 line:85%
<c.yellow>you can switch off everything,</c>

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:41.520 line:91%
<c.yellow>and you can restart
everything. That's okay.</c>

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:43.640 line:91%
<c.yellow>In the case of our
training centre,</c>

00:09:43.640 --> 00:09:46.120 line:91%
<c.yellow>the only one thing
to do is to...</c>

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:50.160 line:91%
<c.yellow>call technical staff
for rescue tugs.</c>

00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:53.320 line:91%
<c.yellow>And quite often,
our models are sent</c>

00:09:53.320 --> 00:09:57.240 line:91%
<c.yellow>directly from the training
centre to our "shipyard"</c>

00:09:57.240 --> 00:09:59.320 line:85%
<c.yellow>for different repairing works.</c>

00:09:59.320 --> 00:10:01.640 line:91%
<c.yellow>And this psychological
effect influences</c>

00:10:01.640 --> 00:10:04.040 line:91%
<c.yellow>very much the
level of education.</c>

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:07.880 line:91%
<c.yellow>People realise everything
a little bit differently</c>

00:10:07.880 --> 00:10:10.200 line:91%
<c.yellow>when comparing with
computer simulators.</c>

00:10:10.200 --> 00:10:12.240 line:91%
<c.cyan>Alright, we are home.</c>
<i>(sighs)</i>

00:10:12.240 --> 00:10:14.640 line:91%
That was a privilege.
Thank you very, very much.

00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:16.280 line:91%
I know very few
people get to do that.

00:10:16.280 --> 00:10:17.680 line:91%
<c.cyan>You're welcome, no problem.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>So thank you so much.</c>

00:10:17.680 --> 00:10:19.600 line:91%
<c.cyan>Here, every
instructor can do that</c>

00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:21.600 line:91%
<i>(laughs)</i>
<c.cyan>...very easily.</c>

